   "since": "2026-09-01",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "The National Gambling Impact Study Commission was established as an independent public advisory commission under authority of PL 104-169 on August 3, 1996.\r\n\r\nThe Commission studied the social and economic impacts of gambling in the United States.\r\n\r\nThe Commission was terminated after submitting its final report in June 1999\r\n\r\nSource: The Encyclopedia of Governmental Advisory Organizations (EGAO 2344, p.336)\r\n",
